cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic research, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Hernández Gualdrón"
    given-names: "Mateo"
title: "TROPICOR: Tropical Correction and Orographic Resolution"
version: 0.1.2
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23219419"
date-released: 2026-10-07
url: "https://github.com/mhgualdron/tropicor"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mhgualdron/tropicor"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - "climate downscaling"
  - "orographic correction"
  - "ERA5 reanalysis"
  - "tropical Andes"
  - "Colombia"
  - "lapse rate"
  - "bias correction"
abstract: >-
  TROPICOR is a Python framework for physics-based vertical downscaling and statistical
  bias correction of global atmospheric reanalyses across complex tropical terrain.
  This software implementation is based on algorithms originally developed during an
  undergraduate geology thesis at Universidad Nacional de Colombia. The author gratefully
  acknowledges the academic guidance and supervision provided by PhD Germán Andrés
  Prieto Gómez and PhD Daniel Hernández Deckers during that original research.
